  CATCHES the log closing a row the queue holds OPEN
  CATCHES an OPEN row whose EVIDENCE cites a DONE neighbour
  QUIET   on a row both records close
  QUIET   on a row the queue closed and the log never announced
  QUIET   on a closed row whose item cell contains an escaped pipe
  QUIET   on a row closed as "REOPENED then DONE"
  QUIET   on a two-column row whose verdict sits in the item cell
  REFUSES on a real divergence
  CATCHES a VALID adjudication (cited line is that row's own DONE) stops the refusal
  CATCHES an UNADJUDICATED divergence still refuses
  CATCHES a BARE marker with no line citation does not silence anything
  CATCHES a citation to a line that is not a DONE line is named and counted
  CATCHES a citation to ANOTHER row's DONE line is named and counted
  CATCHES a citation past the end of the log is named and counted
  CATCHES a pair with no divergence at all still exits 0
  CATCHES an id CLAIMED with no queue row
  QUIET   and ROWLESS alone does NOT change the exit code (the v3 ceiling: the floor is other lanes' rows)
  CATCHES F3: a CLAIM posted before its row exists is NOT gated
  CATCHES a DONE-rowless id THIS tree introduces refuses
  CATCHES an accumulated DONE-rowless id does NOT gate the next committer (H72 scoping)
  CATCHES a BASELINED DONE-rowless id does not gate
  CATCHES and a NON-member of that same baseline still gates
  CATCHES with no git context UNFILED reports without gating (v3 behaviour)
  CATCHES an id DONE with no queue row
  QUIET   on an id the queue does carry
  QUIET   on prefix lines whose subject is not id-shaped
  CATCHES both directions reported from one pass, and the old one still refuses
  CATCHES a CLAIM whose row the queue calls DONE and which the log never closes
  QUIET   and it REPORTS -- an unclosed claim alone never gates
  QUIET   on a CLAIM the log closes
  QUIET   on a CLAIM closed by RETRACTED, not DONE -- the vocabulary is plural
  QUIET   on a RELEASE whose subject is not the first token
  CATCHES on a RELEASE naming TWO subjects -- both close, not just the first
  CATCHES a RELEASE does NOT close a row merely NAMED in its prose
  QUIET   a CLAIM on an OPEN row is never ACCUSED -- that is a live cycle
  CATCHES and it is COUNTED rather than dropped
  QUIET   an unkeyable subject is never scored -- a ROLE never closes
  CATCHES and it is COUNTED rather than dropped
  CATCHES an unknown prefix naming an unclosed claim is reported as DRIFT
  CATCHES a log containing CLAIM from which NONE parse is VOID, never 0 stale
  QUIET   and a VOID run publishes no count at all
selfcheck: both refusing directions fire, every quiet direction stays quiet, ROWLESS reports without gating, and it refuses
